%N A399479 Triangular array read by rows. T(n,k) is the number of labeled acyclic digraphs on [n] that have exactly k isolated points, n>=0, 0<=k<=n.
%C A399479 An isolated point in an acyclic digraph is a vertex with in-degree zero and out-degree zero.
%F A399479 E.g.f.: exp((y-1)*x)*A(x) where A(x) = Sum_{n>=0} A003024(n)*x^n/n!.
%e A399479 Triangle begins:
%e A399479      1;
